# Deploy Rules (CRITICAL — ALWAYS ENFORCED)

## ABSOLUTE RULE: Use the deploy script. No exceptions.

**ALWAYS** run `bash scripts/deploy.sh` from `TripPilot/`.
**NEVER** run `npx wrangler pages deploy` or `npm run build` manually for deployment.

The deploy script handles EVERYTHING:
- Auto-bumps version in ALL 4 files (package.json, app-version.ts, version.json, sw.js)
- Type-checks, builds, creates OTA bundle
- Deploys to Cloudflare Pages on the correct branch (`master`)
- Verifies production is serving the new version
- Verifies OTA bundle is downloadable

Manual deployment WILL break things because the app has 4 version files + a service worker cache name that must ALL be updated atomically. Missing any one = users don't receive the update.

## Deploy commands

```bash
cd TripPilot
bash scripts/deploy.sh              # pages only (default, auto-bumps patch)
bash scripts/deploy.sh all          # pages + worker + apk
bash scripts/deploy.sh pages worker # pages + worker
bash scripts/deploy.sh --dry-run    # preview what would happen
bash scripts/deploy.sh --skip-tests # skip tsc --noEmit (use sparingly)
```

## Before running the script — only ONE thing is needed

**Release notes** — the script will block if missing. Add an entry to `TripPilot/src/utils/release-notes.ts`:
1. Run `bash scripts/deploy.sh --dry-run` to see the target version
2. Add a new entry at the TOP of the `RELEASE_NOTES` array for that version
3. Include `version`, `date` (YYYY-MM-DD), and `items` in all 3 languages (pt-BR, en, es)
4. Write from the USER perspective (what they see/gain, not technical internals)
5. Re-run `bash scripts/deploy.sh`

You do NOT need to manually bump versions — the script does it automatically.

