## Version files (managed by the script — DO NOT bump manually)

| File | Field | Purpose |
|------|-------|---------|
| `package.json` | `version` | npm/build version |
| `src/utils/app-version.ts` | `APP_VERSION` | In-app display version |
| `public/version.json` | `version` + `bundleUrl` | OTA update detection |
| `public/sw.js` | `CACHE_NAME` number | Forces service worker cache bust |

## APK deploy (when native changes exist)

Use `bash scripts/deploy.sh apk` or `bash scripts/deploy.sh all`.
The script handles native version bumps, cap sync, and Gradle build.

APK bump needed when: new Capacitor plugins, AndroidManifest changes, Gradle changes,
new permissions, Firebase config changes, any `TripPilot/android/` modification.

## Post-deploy

- Users receive the update on next page load (service worker detects new cache version)
- Native apps receive OTA within ~30s of cold start
- Verify on phone: Settings → About should show new version

## Forbidden actions

- `npx wrangler pages deploy` outside the script
- Manual `npm run build` for deployment purposes
- Editing version files individually without the script
- Deploying without release notes
